flowchart TD
  classDef works fill:#1d2029,stroke:#555b68,color:#eceef1;
  classDef friction fill:#262a34,stroke:#eceef1,stroke-width:2px,color:#eceef1;
  classDef broken fill:#1d2029,stroke:#d77757,stroke-width:2px,color:#d77757;
  classDef byhand fill:#1d2029,stroke:#eceef1,stroke-width:1px,stroke-dasharray:4 3,color:#eceef1;
  S1["1. VoiceOver on the item says 'tokenpanda, Weekly<br/>28% used, ahead, resets Sunday 17:00'.<br/><i>by hand</i>"]:::byhand
  S2["2. The privacy sentence is one element, and each<br/>window, week and Mac figure is one sentence.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S3["3. Tabs are radio buttons, settings checkboxes<br/>with values, Install, Remove, Quit and the<br/>notifications link buttons with press.<br/><i>by hand</i>"]:::byhand
  S4["4. The keyboard reaches every control: Down and<br/>Up, Left and Right, Space or Return; a thin<br/>accent ring shows where.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S5["5. The key hints read clearly over white, at 4.5<br/>to 1 or more.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S6["6. Reduce motion: the popover opens without<br/>animation.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S7["7. Down also stops on the key figures, and in a<br/>panel shorter than its lines the focused one is<br/>scrolled into view.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S8["8. In a panel capped by a small screen VoiceOver<br/>reads every line, but before macOS 26 its<br/>outline is not shown on a line outside the<br/>visible part, since VoiceOver cannot ask the<br/>app to scroll there.<br/><i>friction</i>"]:::friction
  S1 --> S2
  S2 --> S3
  S3 --> S4
  S4 --> S5
  S5 --> S6
  S6 --> S7
  S7 --> S8
